  "changes": [
    "Shift uses the same native eight-direction running cycles at 11 FPS instead of 9 and moves at 5.9 instead of 4.8 metres per second",
    "Upright lit sprite cards, .48 metre party collision clearance and .5 metre route clearance keep characters out of fixtures and railings",
    "Multiple authored gold floor exits, local-map markers and jade save circles; manual saving removed from the Escape menu",
    "Inns redecorated as travelers lounges with hearths, tables, reading shelves and rest service",
    "Ordinary interactions use small world speech bubbles while main-story conversations retain full portraits",
    "New native party, Ascended, guard and Commander attacks and casting; reviewed full-staff poses and complete wolf tails",
    "Approved horned/quill-maned Duskfang Wolf and bark-armored Briartusk Boar with eight-direction native gait and idle cycles",
    "Contact-timed three-hit chains with melee approach/recovery and layered pooled 3D fire, smoke, ribbons, lightning, ice and wards",
    "Thirteen original ElevenLabs music cues, ten environmental loops and thirty-five effect/foley clips alongside 248 recorded voice performances",
    "Area/battle music, dialogue ducking, spatial water/hearth/weather ambience, running footsteps and independent mix controls",
    "Location-local dense meadows, exact-coordinate construction caches, preaudited thresholds and warmed graphics reduce scene loading",
    "Seven 256 by 256 PixelLab surface textures, two floor markers, stable material variation and new actual game loading photographs",
    "Distinct miniature settlement plans, complete roofs, bridge clearances, stronger wooded groves and an overhead cloud layer",
    "Overhead lighting, matched cloud shadows, rain streaks, wind gusts, fireflies, persistent weather and day/night"
